"""plaguelands_epl_east story pass (22 Nov 2026), to docs/quest_writing_standard.md. Where the giver's speech sat in the accept
line and the journal showed a summary or narration, the speech is now the description and the accept line a new short
beat; the rest were written fresh. Turn-ins untouched."""

STORY = {
    'ple_the_road_between': (
        "I'm Joss Varden. I held Crown Guard's camp until the Dawn talked me into bringing everyone inside these walls, and I'll admit the beds are better. The road between here and Stratholme still needs holding, and it's only open while somebody keeps it open.\n\nThe Blighted Warhorses that used to pull the Crusade's wagons run wild along it now, and the Plague-Rotted Bears come down to the road to eat whatever the horses leave. Thin them both.\n\nOut the gate and west along the road toward the old tower. The horses run the road and the bears keep to the trees beside it. Don't let a horse get behind you, because they kick like they mean it.",
        "Don't let a horse get behind you. They kick like they mean it.",
    ),
    'ple_word_to_lights_hope': (
        "Captain Varden wrote this report and then gave it to me to carry, the same as he did at Crown Guard. Back then I ran it up the road and wondered whether I'd get there. Now it's a walk across the square, and he still won't hand it over himself, because Dawnbringer asks questions.\n\nIt says the Crusade at Tyr's Hand is moving. I'd carry it myself, but the captain wants me on the road watch.\n\nTake it to Commander Eligor Dawnbringer. He stands on the chapel steps at the top of the town. Wait while he reads it, because he'll have something for you.",
        "Wait while he reads it. He'll have something for you.",
    ),
    'ple_darrowshires_ghouls': (
        "Darrowshire was a town in the south-west until the Scourge came for it. The town fought, and lost. The Darrowshire Ghouls that came out of that fight still walk its streets, and on bad nights they walk up the road toward the old tower. I've had two bad nights this month already, and I'd like to put them down before the next one. Darrowshire's a long way west of here, south of the old tower, down the old road, and the ghouls are in the streets and the yards.",
        "Mind the ghosts in Darrowshire. They're still fighting a battle that ended years ago.",
    ),
    'ple_the_houndmasters': (
        "The Crusade at Tyr's Hand sends its hounds up the road at night, and the Tyr's Hand Houndmasters who run them know exactly where my sentries stand. I lost two good people last week.\n\nI want the houndmasters dead, and I'd like their dogs to have nobody to come home to.\n\nTyr's Hand is on the coast, south of the chapel down the road. The houndmasters keep to the kennels at the north end. Kill the handlers and the hounds won't know what to do.",
        "Kill the handlers, and the hounds won't know what to do.",
    ),
    'ple_arrows_on_the_road': (
        "With the hounds gone, the Crusade's sent its archers instead. Every Tyr's Hand Marksman on the walls shoots at anything on the coast road, and my wagons can't get through that way.\n\nClear the walls. The marksmen stand on Tyr's Hand's walls and in its towers. Get close fast, because they won't come down to you, and don't stop in the open.",
        "Get close fast, and don't stop in the open.",
    ),
    'ple_the_blackwood_shore': (
        "I'm Ines, and I keep the water clean, which out here means I keep everyone alive. The chapel's well is good, but it isn't enough for everyone Crown Guard brought with it, so we haul the rest from Blackwood Lake.\n\nThe Blackwood Drowned walk out of that lake every night and foul the shore where I fill the barrels. I'd like to do my job without a sword in my other hand.\n\nThe lake's north-west of here, in the middle of the country. The drowned come up out of the shallows. Stay on the dry ground if you can, because they're stronger in the water and they'll try to pull you in.",
        "Stay on dry ground. They'll try to pull you in.",
    ),
    'ple_whats_in_the_water': (
        "I want to know how the plague gets into Blackwood Lake, and I think the Blackwood Snapjaws can tell me. They swallow stones to grind their food, and the stones soak up whatever's in the water. They're a record, if you know how to read them.\n\nThe snapjaws sun themselves on the shore. The stones are in the gizzard, which is exactly where it sounds like. I'm sorry, and thank you.",
        "The stones are in the gizzard. I'm sorry, and thank you.",
    ),
    'ple_the_blackwood_drowner': (
        "Something sits on the bottom of Blackwood Lake and bleeds plague into the silt. The Drowned call it the Blackwood Drowner, and the Blackwood Snapjaws won't go near the deep water where it lies. I've read its silt in every gizzard stone you brought me. Drag it out and end it, and the lake will start to clear on its own. It comes up from the deep end when it's hungry, so thin the snapjaws on the shore while you wait.",
        "When it pulls you under, don't panic. Fight your way back to the shallows.",
    ),
    'ple_filters_for_felwood': (
        "I've drawn up a filter, sand and charcoal and a bit of cleverness, that takes the plague out of Blackwood's water. I've heard there's a forest across the sea, Felwood, where the water's poisoned with something worse. They've got a carpenter at the Emerald Sanctuary, Tomasz Wolny, who builds whatever the druids need.\n\nI'd like him to build this.\n\nTake the zeppelin from Tirisfal to Orgrimmar, then north through Ashenvale to Felwood. The Sanctuary's the clean glade in the middle of it. Tomasz will be the one hammering something.",
        'Tomasz will be the one hammering something.',
    ),
    'ple_horse_for_the_pot': (
        "The wagons come when they come, and the chapel's got a lot more mouths since Crown Guard moved in. I've found that the Blighted Warhorses on the road are sick on the outside and mostly fine on the inside, if you're careful.\n\nI want the meat, and I don't want to hear about it.\n\nThe horses run the road west of the gate. Cut from the flank, where the meat's thickest. Don't tell anyone what's in the stew, and I won't either.",
        "Cut from the flank, and don't tell anyone what's in the stew.",
    ),
    'ple_a_barrel_for_sorrow_hill': (
        "I brew a dark ale out of whatever the wagons bring, and the woman who cooks for the Order of the Pale Flame, Priya Raman, wrote to say she'd trade me a recipe for a barrel. Nobody's ever offered me a recipe for ale before.\n\nI'd like the barrel taken west, and the recipe brought back in your head. Don't write it down. Recipes get stolen.\n\nThe Order's camped inside the Bulwark now, at the far west of the Plaguelands where the road comes in from Tirisfal. It's a long way, so fly if you can. And don't drink it on the way, because I'll know.",
        "Don't drink it on the way, because I'll know.",
    ),
    'ple_wild_bats': (
        "The Dawn's riding bats are healthy, and Aldous and I mean to keep them that way. The Carrion Bats that roost in the dead trees round the chapel carry the plague, and they've started fighting ours for the perch.\n\nI want the wild ones gone.\n\nThey roost all round the chapel and they're out every evening. Ours have blue tags on their legs, so please don't hit those.",
        "Ours have blue tags on their legs. Please don't hit those.",
    ),
    'ple_a_bat_for_lights_hope': (
        "Aldous lost two bats to the Mossflayers this month, and I've got a young female who's ready to fly. I raised her at Crown Guard. She's the best one I've got.\n\nShe's in the covered basket. Take her across to Aldous at the perch on the east side of town, gently. It's not far, and I'd do it myself, but if she sees me hand her over she'll follow me home.\n\nKeep the cover on, because she'll try to fly back if she sees the sky.",
        "Keep the cover on, or she'll try to fly back to me.",
    ),
    'ple_tyrs_hand': (
        "The Scarlet Crusade holds Tyr's Hand, a walled town on the coast south of here. They think the Dawn are traitors for taking in anyone who'll fight, and they've said so, loudly, from the walls.\n\nI'd rather talk, and they won't, so I want the Tyr's Hand Crusaders on those walls thinned before they come north.\n\nGo out the gate and south down the road to the coast. The crusaders walk the streets and the walls. They'll fight to the last, so don't expect any of them to run.",
        "They'll fight to the last. Don't expect any of them to run.",
    ),
    'ple_the_abbots': (
        "Tyr's Hand's crusaders fight because the Tyr's Hand Abbots tell them to. The abbots preach in the town's chapels every morning, and every morning the crusaders come out ready to die. I've listened to those sermons from the walls, and they're very good, which is the problem. Stop the preaching, and the fighting will lose its heart. The abbots keep to the chapels and the cloister in the middle of the town.",
        "They heal each other, so take them one at a time and don't let them gather.",
    ),
    'ple_abbot_varenne': (
        "Abbot Varenne rules Tyr's Hand. He was a priest of the Light in Lordaeron before the plague, and he's the one who decided that anyone who came from somewhere else was a servant of the dead.\n\nWe studied together at Northshire, a long time ago. He was kinder then. I'd like it finished, and I'd like it to be somebody who doesn't remember that.\n\nHe holds the great chapel at the heart of Tyr's Hand, and he doesn't fight alone. Go in with friends, and watch for the fire when he calls it down.",
        'Go in with friends, and watch for the fire when he calls it down.',
    ),
    'ple_a_word_with_the_order': (
        "The Commander's written to the Order of the Pale Flame, and I wrote it down for him. They're Scarlets who walked out of the Crusade, and they kill only the mindless dead. Some of the Dawn don't trust them. He'd like to, and so would I.\n\nTheir Flamekeeper, Rory Callahan, knows the Crusade from the inside. The Commander wants to talk to him about Tyr's Hand, and about Hearthglen.\n\nThey're camped inside the Bulwark now, at the far west of the Plaguelands. It's a long way, so fly. Give it to Rory and tell him the Commander would like an answer, not a sermon.",
        'Tell Rory the Commander wants an answer, not a sermon.',
    ),
    'ple_marrow_of_the_scar': (
        "I break down the Scourgestones that come to the chapel, and lately I've found something new in them. It's coming from the Pestilent Scar, where the Scourge is building with bone.\n\nThe Scar Bone Constructs that walk there are full of a cold grey marrow. I'd like some of it, carefully.\n\nThe Scar's north-west of the chapel, a long gash in the ground full of bones. Cut the marrow from the big bones in their legs, and don't hold it any longer than you have to.",
        "From the big leg bones, and don't hold it longer than you must.",
    ),
    'ple_the_bone_colossus': (
        "At the bottom of the Pestilent Scar the Scourge is building a giant out of the bones of everyone who died in the east. I call it the Bone Colossus. That's what the marrow was for.\n\nThe Scar Bone Constructs guard it while it grows. I want it pulled down before it's finished.\n\nIt stands in the deepest part of the Scar. It's slow, and it's very, very strong. Kill the constructs first, then take it with every friend you can find.",
        'Constructs first, then the colossus with every friend you can find.',
    ),
    'ple_darrowshires_dead': (
        "I'm Ysolde, and I keep the chapel's prayers for the dead, all of them, because nobody else in the east will.\n\nDarrowshire's dead never got any prayers. The Darrowshire Spirits are still fighting the battle that killed them, every night, over and over, and they don't know it's over.\n\nDarrowshire's far to the west, south of the old tower. The spirits fight in the town square and on the road in. They'll take you for the enemy, so be ready. Set them free.",
        "They'll take you for the enemy. Set them free anyway.",
    ),
    'ple_the_pestilent_scar': (
        "I won't send anyone into a place I haven't heard described, and nobody's come back from the Pestilent Scar with a straight story. One man said fire, one said ice, one wouldn't say anything.\n\nWalk to its edge and look. Don't go down.\n\nIt's north-west of the chapel, past the lake. You'll smell it before you see it. Stand at the edge and look, and then come straight back here.",
        "Stand at the edge and look. Don't go down.",
    ),
    'ple_the_shadowhunters': (
        "Somebody's been hexing the chapel. I've found little bundles of feathers and teeth under the pews. The only ones in the east who'd do that are the Mossflayer Shadowhunters of Zul'Mashar.\n\nI'd like them dead before they get bolder. The dead don't cross this ground, but the living do.\n\nZul'Mashar's in the far north-east, past Quel'Lithien Lodge. The shadowhunters keep to the temple steps. Their hexes are nasty, so get a priest to look at you when you're back.",
        "Get a priest to look at you when you're back. Their hexes linger.",
    ),
    'ple_hex_fetishes': (
        "The hex bundles under the pews were tied round scraps of the chapel's own laundry. Somebody inside these walls has been stealing from us for the Mossflayers.\n\nThe Mossflayer Shadowhunters still carry their fetishes. I want to see whose cloth is in them.\n\nThey carry them on their belts at Zul'Mashar. Bring them back unopened. I'll know the cloth when I see it.",
        "Bring them back unopened. I'll know the cloth when I see it.",
    ),
    'ple_troll_medicine': (
        "I'm Marisol, and I run the infirmary. I've got more patients than beds. If you're bleeding, sit down. If you're not, listen.\n\nThe Mossflayer trolls heal faster than anybody else in the Plaguelands. Their scouts carry herb pouches, and I want to know what's in them. I'm not too proud to learn from a troll.\n\nZul'Mashar's in the far north-east. The Mossflayer Scouts range out from the temple in pairs. Bring me the pouches closed, because I want to see how they pack them.",
        'Bring the pouches closed. I want to see how they pack them.',
    ),
    'ple_mossflayer_raiders': (
        "My wagons bring the wounded in from the road, and the Mossflayers have started raiding them. The Mossflayer Warriors hit the wagons from the trees, and the Mossflayer Scouts pick off whoever runs.\n\nI want the road safe for people who are already hurt.\n\nThey come down from Zul'Mashar to the north road. Go up there and hit them at home. They're fast and they're angry, so don't fight more than you can handle.",
        "Hit them at home, and don't take on more than you can handle.",
    ),
    'ple_zulmashar_the_last': (
        "The Mossflayers follow a warlord who named himself after their city. Zul'Mashar the Last says he's the last of the old Amani blood, and he's sworn to drive everyone who isn't a troll out of these lands. I've patched up enough of his raiders' work to know he means it. The raids won't stop while he's giving the orders. He holds the top of the temple at Zul'Mashar, north of here, and he hits like a falling tree.",
        "Take friends, and bring bandages. You'll need them, and I'll need you back.",
    ),
    'ple_the_medics_network': (
        "The medics who came through keep in touch across the sea as best we can. Letters, mostly, carried by whoever's going that way.\n\nI've written up what the Mossflayer herbs do. There's a paramedic at Talonbranch Glade in Felwood, Marcus Oyelaran, treating burns up there that sound exactly like the ones I'm treating here.\n\nTake the zeppelin from Tirisfal to Orgrimmar, then go north through Ashenvale to Felwood and up to Talonbranch at the top. Marcus will be the one with his sleeves rolled up. Don't let the notes get wet.",
        "Don't let the notes get wet on the way.",
    ),
    'ple_the_restless_lodge': (
        "I'm Faelis, and I served at Quel'Lithien Lodge, in the north, where my people kept watch on Lordaeron's border. The lodge fell with everything else. Everyone I served with is still there, and none of them are resting.\n\nThe Restless Lodge Rangers still walk their posts. I knew every one of them. I'm asking you to let them rest.\n\nThe lodge is in the north, past the lake. They'll be on the walls and in the trees, where they always stood. They still shoot straight, so keep moving.",
        'They still shoot straight, so keep moving.',
    ),
    'ple_the_silver_leaves': (
        "Every ranger of Quel'Lithien carried a silver leaf on a green cord, a token from Quel'Thalas. I'd like to send them home, so that somebody there knows their names.\n\nThe Restless Lodge Rangers still walk Quel'Lithien Lodge, north-west of here, and they still wear them round their necks. Bring back what you find. Not every one of them will still have theirs, and I'm sorry for that.",
        'Not all of them will still have theirs. Bring what you find.',
    ),
    'ple_ranger_lord_saelith': (
        "Ranger-Lord Saelith commanded Quel'Lithien Lodge. He was my captain and my friend, and he died holding the gate. He still holds it, and he still kills anyone who comes through.\n\nI can't do it myself. I've stood at that gate with an arrow on the string and I couldn't loose it. I'm asking you.\n\nHe stands at the lodge's inner gate, where he fell. He's fast and he doesn't miss. Go with friends, and close the distance quickly.",
        "Close the distance quickly. He doesn't miss.",
    ),
    'ple_lamp_oil': (
        "I'm Jessa, and I keep the beds and the lamps. The lamps stay lit all night, because the dead don't like the light, and since Crown Guard moved in I've twice as many lamps and the same amount of oil.\n\nThe Plague-Rotted Bears carry fat under the rot that renders down clean. I've tried it.\n\nThey wander the woods all round the chapel. Cut the fat from the back, where the rot's thinnest. It won't smell nice, and I'm sorry about that.",
        "Cut from the back, where the rot's thinnest.",
    ),
    'ple_pamelas_doll': (
        "Hello, are you here to see Daddy? He's out at the fight, but he'll be back soon.\n\nI'm Pamela, and I've lost Dolly, and I've looked everywhere. The Darrowshire Ghouls took her, they did! I saw one carry her off. They're all over the town and they won't give her back.\n\nShe's got a blue dress and one button eye. Will you find her for me, please?",
        "She's got a blue dress and one button eye!",
    ),
    'ple_a_letter_for_auntie': (
        "I wrote a letter to Auntie Marlene! She lives out west, near the big town. I haven't heard from her in ever so long.\n\nA man came through and said there are kind people in the west who keep a book with everybody's names in it. If anyone knows where Auntie is, it's them.\n\nThe lady with the book is in the big wall at the end of the road, where the road goes out of the Plaguelands. You'll be ever so careful with it, won't you?",
        "You'll be ever so careful with it, won't you?",
    ),
    'ple_where_daddy_is': (
        "Daddy's at the big fight, south of the houses. He's been there ever so long. I can see the flags from the end of the road, but I'm not allowed to go.\n\nHe's Captain Joseph Redpath, and he's very brave. Everybody says so.\n\nWill you go and find him? Tell him I've been good, and that I've got Dolly back, and that I'm waiting. Tell him he can come home now.",
        "Tell him I've been good. Tell him he can come home now.",
    ),
    'ple_the_bones_of_the_east': (
        "I dug coal in the Rhondda, back home, so when Ysolde found out where the east's dead were going, she sent for me. The Scourge has dug a mine under the Pestilent Scar. The Bone Miners in it are digging up the dead to build its constructs, and the Scourge Pit Guards keep them at it.\n\nI want the digging stopped. It's a bad mine, badly propped, and what they're digging up is people.\n\nThe mine's in the hill under the Scar, north-west of here. Every gallery's deeper than the last, so it's a long walk down. The pit guards will keep you out if they can.",
        "It's a long walk down, and the pit guards won't make it shorter.",
    ),
    'ple_the_overseer': (
        "The tallies on the pit walls all end at one place. Overseer Marrowgrim sits in the pit at the bottom with a meat hook and a cart, and nothing leaves that mine that he hasn't weighed. We had a man like that at the colliery, and he was a lot less dangerous.\n\nI want him dead before the Scourge has bone enough for another colossus.\n\nHe's in the marrow pit at the end of the deepest gallery. He's big and he's slow until he isn't, so don't stand where that hook can reach you, and watch out for the cart.",
        "Don't stand where that hook can reach you, and mind the cart.",
    ),
    'ple_the_ossifier': (
        "I've found a workshop off the middle of the Bone Mines, and Marrowgrim's tallies say everything the mine digs up goes there first. The Ossifier is a necromancer, and he's the one who turns the east's dead into the Scourge's constructs.\n\nClose his workshop, and I'll bring the roof down on it after.\n\nIt's off the middle gallery, up a short passage. He'll be wearing bone armour, and it's thick, so be patient with it. Break that first, then break him.",
        'Break the bone armour first, then break him.',
    ),
    'ple_hammerfalls_answer': (
        "Everything that crosses Arathi crosses in front of me. Lately that's been the Argent Dawn's carts heading east, and the Dawn has asked Hammerfall for steel.\n\nI've written my answer. I want it carried by somebody who'll fight their way there, because a messenger who can't won't arrive.\n\nGo north to the Plaguelands and take the road east as far as it runs. Light's Hope is at the end of it, behind its own gate. Tell the commander Hammerfall keeps its word, and don't stop to fight anything you can walk past.",
        "Don't stop to fight anything you can walk past.",
    ),
}
